  "system": {
    "slug": "mystaria-stage-4",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 12
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>At Stage IV — the final threshold before full Phantom conversion — Mystaria is more machine than human. Her monofilament blade has been upgraded to Phantom specification, her phase cloak performance is indistinguishable from a full conversion, and cybernetic threading throughout her musculature provides reflexes that border on prescience. She retains enough of her original cunning to operate with tactical flexibility rather than robotic compliance. Only the final neural overwrite separates her from a full Cerberus Phantom.</p><p><strong>Sneak Attack:</strong> Mystaria deals an extra 3d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p><p><strong>Phase Cloak (1 action, 1/encounter):</strong> Mystaria becomes Invisible and gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC until the end of her next turn or until she makes a Strike.</p><p><strong>Cybernetic Threading:</strong> Mystaria has a +5-foot speed bonus and a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 70 Shield HP. Recharges 25 HP per turn.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
